          "id": "item_1",
          "type": "agent_message",
          "text": "- **High \u2014 Rejected create dispatch can leave cleanup permanently unresolved.**  \n  **Evidence:** `packages/workflow-control/src/specialistLauncher.ts`, `#launch` and `#settleOwned`.  \n  The launcher persists `create_pending` before `dispatchSchedulerContainer` performs document verification and the new synchronous admission check. If either rejects, Docker creation never starts. Cleanup nevertheless treats an absent container as ambiguous forever. Recovery exhausts its budget without a supported resolution. The supplied regressions invalidate admission only before **start**, after creation succeeded.  \n  **Correction:** Distinguish a definitively rejected dispatch from an initiated but uncertain create, with durable bookkeeping that preserves crash safety. Add a regression expiring admission inside create-boundary verification; assert no create call and successful containment settlement.\n\n- **Medium \u2014 Malformed runtime JSON still receives cleanup diagnostics.**  \n  **Evidence:** `packages/workflow-control/src/developmentHost.ts`, `#attachRuntime`, `classifyDevelopmentError`; `packages/workflow-control/test/developmentHostJournal.test.ts`.  \n  The JSON correction covers the operator configuration in `runDevelopmentCommand`. The optional runtime configuration still uses unguarded `JSON.parse(runtimeBytes)`. A syntax error becomes `cleanup_pending`, yielding exit code 4 instead of invalid-configuration exit code 2. The supplied JSON test exercises only the operator file.  \n  **Correction:** Explicitly classify runtime JSON parsing failures as `invalid_configuration`; add a CLI test supplying valid operator configuration and malformed runtime JSON.\n\n- **Medium \u2014 Status can report ready after admission freshness expires.**  \n  **Evidence:** `packages/workflow-control/src/developmentHost.ts`, `developmentStatus`; `packages/workflow-control/src/developmentHostJournal.ts`, `assertDevelopmentAdmission`.  \n  Admission rejects observations older than five seconds, but status invalidates persisted `ready` only when the fifteen-second owner lease expires. A stalled supervisor can therefore report effective readiness while dispatch would reject it. Topology freshness is held only in memory and cannot be assessed by the status command.  \n  **Correction:** Persist the readiness/topology validity deadline and apply it consistently to admission and status. Test status during a supervisor stall after readiness expires but before ownership expires.\n\nThe supplied generation transcript addresses review13\u2019s missing current-image generation evidence. Hosted gates remain explicitly pending. The source findings above prevent a \u201cno remaining actionable blockers\u201d conclusion.\n\nEvidence-only review; no commands executed or state changed. This is not human approval."
        }
